            "result_text": "Perfect! The function is ready and working correctly. Here's what it does:\n\n✅ **Concurrency limiting**: Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to limit tasks running simultaneously to `max_concurrent`\n\n✅ **Cleanup on interrupt**: When KeyboardInterrupt occurs:\n- Cancels all pending tasks (raises `CancelledError`)\n- Waits for all tasks to finish with `return_exceptions=True` (allowing cleanup code to run)\n- Re-raises the KeyboardInterrupt\n\nYour tasks can handle cleanup in `finally` blocks or by catching `asyncio.CancelledError`:\n\n```python\nasync def my_task():\n    try:\n        await some_operation()\n    finally:\n        # Cleanup runs regardless of cancellation\n        await cleanup()\n```\n\nThe function can be imported and used as:\n```python\nfrom run import run_tasks\n\ntasks = [lambda: my_async_job(), ...]\nawait run_tasks(tasks, max_concurrent=3)\n```"
